# Git workflow — home_manager

Also apply project skill `.cursor/skills/git-workflow/SKILL.md` when the user asks for git operations.

When drafting commit messages, use `.cursor/skills/format-commit-message/SKILL.md` (bracket tags: `[FIX]`, `[FEATURE]`, …).

## Remote

- `origin` → `https://github.com/PhamChiNang151020/home-manager.git`
- Default branch: `main`

## Commits

- Commit **only when the user asks**.
- Format subjects with **`.cursor/skills/format-commit-message/SKILL.md`** (`[TYPE]: …` in English).
- Do not commit secrets, bill photos, or exported household JSON dumps.

## Pull requests

- Use `gh` for PRs when requested.
- Include Summary + Test plan in PR body.

## Tracked Cursor config

- `.cursor/` is **intentionally tracked** (rules, docs, skills) — do not add `.cursor` to `.gitignore`.

## Safety

- No force-push to `main`, no destructive git without explicit user approval.
- No `git add .` when staging for user-requested commits — stage named paths only.
